From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TBI Lab runtime <runtime@tbi-lab.local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] hw/i2c/esp32_i2c, hw/misc/tbi_bridge, hw/xtensa/esp32:
 I2C to the TBI host
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TBI Lab (Sprint 12, ADR-011 §4). The ESP32 I2C controller executes its
command list against the TBI host: every bus phase goes to tbi-bridge as
"B <vns> <bus> S|W|R|P ..." and is answered synchronously (K for START
and written bytes, D for read bytes). Without a bridge nothing
acknowledges and reads see the released bus (0xff). tbi-bridge announces
the i2c capability.

The upstream TMP105 temperature sensor at 0x48 on I2C0 is no longer
created: it is not part of any user's circuit.

Controller changes, each proven necessary by the Sprint 12 R3 probe or
required by PM decision D-9:
- a NACKed data byte with ACK checking enabled raises ACK_ERR and stops
  the command list, as an address NACK does (upstream ignored it);
- RSTART is a repeated START (the transaction is not ended);
- bus timing: the command list's duration is computed from the timing
  registers the driver programmed (80 MHz module clock; 9 SCL periods of
  SCL_LOW_PERIOD + SCL_HIGH_PERIOD per byte, RSTART_SETUP + START_HOLD
  per START, STOP_SETUP + STOP_HOLD per STOP); ACK_ERR, TRANS_COMPLETE,
  END_DETECT and the DONE bits are raised when it has elapsed and the
  bus reads busy until then. The SCL filter, rise-time stretch, clock
  stretching and arbitration are not modelled.

Signed-off-by: TBI Lab <runtime@tbi-lab.local>
